From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reelee81 <reelee81@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:41:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/18] fitz: Decode JPX images at reduced resolution when they
 will be scaled down.

compressed_image_get_pixmap() always decoded JPX images at full resolution
and only subsampled the result afterwards, so a thumbnail of a page with a
10200x14031 JPX image needed about 2 GB of memory. The JPX branch now passes
the requested l2factor to OpenJPEG (opj_set_decoded_resolution_factor),
limited to the number of resolution levels in the codestream, and reports
the applied factor back like the JPEG branch does.

The reduction is not used for indexed images, for JP2 files with a palette
box (the palette is applied to the decoded indices), or for images with a
colour key. If decoding at the reduced resolution fails, the image is
decoded again at full resolution.

Modified for ReePDF on 2026-11-08.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
